From d0d8ff90f395389c009a558fc0c225f8427ece26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:15:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bugs found reviewing JukaMix: service stop, NGPC icon,
 WonderSwan scraping, FW restore cancel

- Tailscale / SFTPGo / Syncthing menu scripts stopped their daemon with pkill
  <full path>. pkill matches the process name, so the path never matched: "Disable"
  left the service running and "Enable" started a duplicate. Use pkill -x <name>.
  The Tailscale scripts also set TAILSCALE to the tailscaled daemon, so
  "$TAILSCALE down" ran "tailscaled down" and the download check never looked for
  the tailscale CLI. TAILSCALE now points to the tailscale CLI.
- Add icons on best folders: the second NGP) case label (Neo Geo Pocket Color) could
  never match, so the NGC folder (Neo Geo Pocket Color in CrossMix) got no icon.
  Renamed to NGC).
- ScreenScraper ids: WS and WSC were mapped to 207 (Watara Supervision), which also
  shadowed the real WonderSwan entry below. 207 now belongs to SUPERVISION; WSC uses
  the WonderSwan id already used for WS (45); removed the unreachable SFX=19 line.
- FW Settings Save-Load: cancelling the backup file chooser tested a variable that
  was never assigned ($cleaned_input), so B ended in "Backup archive not found".
  It now tests the selector output and exits cleanly.

tests/jukamix_fixes_test.sh covers each item (35 checks; 17 fail on the old code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
